{
  "$comment": "E7 (#VAPP-270, epic #VAPP-259; docs/spec/apps.md §13.3, runner.json `bundle`): `exponential bundle`, the CLI that exports a signed package to native binaries on the prebuilt runners. Rust only (`apps/desktop/crates/eengine-bundle`, `tests/fixture.rs` replays every case; the CLI subcommand is `crates/cli` `bundle`). NOTHING IS COMPILED PER APP except iOS (the Mac lane links only the declared capability modules, ITMS-90683). THE STEPS, in order: (1) PREPARE (`prepareCases`, `prepare(file, bundleToml, options)` -> `{ok: {package, config, scopes}} | {refused: {code, detail}}`, the first refusal wins in this order): the file is not JSON = `notJson`; its signature does not verify = `signature`; unsigned (no `signature`) = `unsigned` unless `--allow-unsigned`; the package's `catalogId` is one of `refuse.catalogs` (the Exponential-app catalog: `exponential.*` actions and the in-app shapes exist only inside Exponential) = `catalog`; a declared capability scope that is `hostOnly` in capabilities.json (`shell.edit`) or unknown = `capability` (detail = the scope); genUI refuses the package (eengine `package::validate`) = `invalid`; bundle.toml's `config.keys` read through runner.json's `runnerConfig` (its issues = `config`, detail `<key>:<code>` joined by `,`; any key outside `config.keys` + `config.sections` is an issue too, so no update feed, telemetry or account can be configured). `scopes` = the package's `capabilities[].id` sorted, de-duplicated. (2) RUNNER: the prebuilt runner kit per target (`kits`): `--runners <dir>` (a workspace build, `scripts/runner-kits.sh`) or the release assets of the pinned `eengine-v<eengine version>` (`kits.release`; each asset's sha256 is checked against its `.sha256` asset). A kit missing its `NOTICES.txt` is refused (`notices`): every export ships the third-party notices of what it runs. (3) INJECT: `app/` = runner.json `bundle` (`package.app.json` byte for byte as given, `runner.json` = the prepared config as `{id, name, version, network}`), at the target's runner.json `bundle.locations`; the icons (`icons`, rendered from the one SVG at every size the target asks for); the platform manifest. (4) PERMISSIONS (`permissions`, `permissionCases`, `platformManifest(target, scopes, config, purposes)`): ONLY what the declared scopes ask for, never more: Android `<uses-permission>` lines between the template's `E7:PERMISSIONS` markers (+ INTERNET when `network` is not `off`); iOS the capability MODULES to link and the Info.plist purpose strings, each = the scope's `why` from the package (else `purposeFallback` with the app name); macOS the sandbox entitlements (`base` always + per scope + `network.client` when `network` is not `off`) and the URL scheme; Linux the `.desktop` entry (`Exec=<bin> %u`, `MimeType=x-scheme-handler/<scheme>;`); Windows the URL protocol under `HKCU\\\\Software\\\\Classes\\\\<scheme>` written by the installer; the web manifest fields (no permissions: every web capability is a picker or asks in the page). The URL scheme is the config id (runner.json: deep links are `<config id>://<screen>?<params>`). (5) SIGN (`signing`): with the AUTHOR's own keys from bundle.toml `[signing.<target>]` or the environment; we never hold them. Without them the output is ad-hoc (macOS `codesign -s -`, iOS unsigned .ipa for re-signing) or unsigned (Windows, Linux) and the CLI says so; Android without a keystore signs with a throwaway debug key and says the .apk is for testing only. (6) OUT (`outputs`): the files per target under `--out` (default `dist/`). NO updater, NO update feed, NO telemetry, NO account: a new package version is a rebundle.",
  "command": "exponential bundle <package.app.json> --icon <icon.svg> --config <bundle.toml> --target <targets,comma separated> [--runners <dir>] [--out <dir>] [--allow-unsigned]",
  "targets": [
    "macos",
    "windows",
    "linux",
    "android",
    "ios",
    "web"
  ],
  "refuse": {
    "catalogs": [
      "https://ui.exponential.at/catalogs/exponential-app/v1"
    ]
  },
  "config": {
    "file": "bundle.toml",
    "keys": [
      "id",
      "name",
      "version",
      "network"
    ],
    "sections": [
      "signing"
    ]
  },
  "kits": {
    "dir": "<runners>/<target>",
    "release": "https://github.com/Niach/exponential/releases/download/eengine-v{version}/eengine-runner-kit-{target}.tar.gz",
    "notices": "NOTICES.txt"
  },
  "icons": {
    "macos": [
      16,
      32,
      64,
      128,
      256,
      512,
      1024
    ],
    "windows": [
      16,
      24,
      32,
      48,
      64,
      256
    ],
    "linux": [
      32,
      48,
      64,
      128,
      256,
      512
    ],
    "android": {
      "mdpi": 48,
      "hdpi": 72,
      "xhdpi": 96,
      "xxhdpi": 144,
      "xxxhdpi": 192
    },
    "ios": [
      1024
    ],
    "web": [
      192,
      512
    ]
  },
  "outputs": {
    "macos": [
      "{name}.app",
      "{name}-{version}.dmg"
    ],
    "windows": [
      "{name}-{version}-setup.exe"
    ],
    "linux": [
      "{id}_{version}_{arch}.deb",
      "{name}-{version}-{arch}.AppImage"
    ],
    "android": [
      "{name}-{version}.apk",
      "{name}-{version}.aab"
    ],
    "ios": [
      "{name}-{version}.ipa"
    ],
    "web": [
      "{name}-{version}-web/"
    ]
  },
  "permissions": {
    "android": {
      "scopes": {
        "photos.read": [
          "<uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.READ_MEDIA_IMAGES\" />",
          "<uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.READ_MEDIA_VISUAL_USER_SELECTED\" />",
          "<uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE\" android:maxSdkVersion=\"32\" />"
        ],
        "notifications.post": [
          "<uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS\" />",
          "<uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED\" />"
        ]
      },
      "network": [
        "<uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.INTERNET\" />"
      ],
      "markers": [
        "<!-- E7:PERMISSIONS -->",
        "<!-- /E7:PERMISSIONS -->"
      ]
    },
    "ios": {
      "modules": {
        "photos.read": "ExponentialEnginePhotos",
        "files.read": "ExponentialEngineFiles",
        "files.write": "ExponentialEngineFiles",
        "share.send": "ExponentialEngineShare",
        "print.pdf": "ExponentialEnginePrint",
        "notifications.post": "ExponentialEngineNotifications"
      },
      "purposes": {
        "photos.read": "NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription",
        "share.send": "NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription"
      },
      "purposeFallback": {
        "NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription": "{name} opens the photos you pick.",
        "NSPhotoLibraryAddUsageDescription": "{name} saves images you share."
      }
    },
    "macos": {
      "base": [
        "com.apple.security.app-sandbox"
      ],
      "scopes": {
        "photos.read": [
          "com.apple.security.assets.pictures.read-only",
          "com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only"
        ],
        "files.read": [
          "com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-only"
        ],
        "files.write": [
          "com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write"
        ],
        "print.pdf": [
          "com.apple.security.print"
        ]
      },
      "network": [
        "com.apple.security.network.client"
      ]
    },
    "linux": {
      "exec": "{bin} %u",
      "mimeType": "x-scheme-handler/{scheme};",
      "categories": "Utility;"
    },
    "windows": {
      "protocolKey": "HKCU\\Software\\Classes\\{scheme}"
    },
    "web": {
      "display": "standalone",
      "startUrl": "./",
      "scope": "./",
      "color": "#09090b"
    }
  },
  "signing": {
    "macos": {
      "inputs": [
        "identity (Developer ID Application)",
        "notary: rcodesign API key JSON (issuer id, key id, .p8)"
      ],
      "fallback": "adhoc"
    },
    "windows": {
      "inputs": [
        "osslsigncode: certificate (.pfx) + password",
        "or Azure Trusted Signing: endpoint, account, profile"
      ],
      "fallback": "unsigned"
    },
    "linux": {
      "inputs": [],
      "fallback": "unsigned"
    },
    "android": {
      "inputs": [
        "keystore (.jks/.p12), alias, store + key passwords"
      ],
      "fallback": "debugKey"
    },
    "ios": {
      "inputs": [
        "DEVELOPMENT_TEAM",
        "distribution certificate + provisioning profile (TestFlight)"
      ],
      "fallback": "unsigned"
    },
    "web": {
      "inputs": [],
      "fallback": "none"
    }
  },
